WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.138
NIST SP 800-53 plays a central role in the Risk Management Framework,

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.397
often called RMF.

00:00:06.397 --> 00:00:11.434
Organizations use the control catalog when selecting and implementing safeguards during system

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.533
authorization and ongoing risk management.

00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:18.151
The RMF provides a process for preparing, categorizing systems, selecting controls,

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.670
implementing controls, assessing controls, authorizing systems,

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.769
and monitoring controls over time.

00:00:22.769 --> 00:00:28.226
SP 800-53 has also influenced programs such as FedRAMP, state government security initiatives,

00:00:28.226 --> 00:00:30.325
and many private-sector compliance efforts.

00:00:30.325 --> 00:00:37.042
The publication is most useful when treated as part of a broader governance and engineering process,

00:00:37.042 --> 00:00:40.820
not as a document that solves compliance by itself.
